cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use link, please cite it by its DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.23264990.
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'link: Develop, Test and Communicate Intrinsic Habitat and Connectivity Models
  for the BC Freshwater Atlas Stream Network'
version: 0.68.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23264990
abstract: 'Tools for developing, testing and communicating intrinsic habitat models
  on stream networks: where each fish species could spawn and rear, and which of that
  habitat fish can reach. Current models rate habitat from stream gradient, channel
  width and discharge, resolve access past natural barriers, and record the road and
  rail crossings and dams below each reach. Every rule and threshold is a row in a
  config, so models can be changed, compared, checked against fish observations and
  traced to the rules that produced them. Runs on the British Columbia Freshwater
  Atlas through ''fresh''. Under active development.'
